From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 22:22:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 190/190] Sega CD: there is no warm boot here, so stop
 pretending there is

Every start reads the whole OS image off the disc or out of the
cartridge, so the code that is running has never run before. What does
survive a reset is sub PRG-RAM -- the console does not clear it -- and
_warm_magic sits in it, at a .w address in low memory. So EmuTOS read
back the magic a previous run had written and concluded this was a warm
boot.

That is wrong on its face here, and it has two consequences. The visible
one is the welcome screen: show_initinfo is FIRST_BOOT, so a reset came
up with no EmuTOS splash at all. The quieter one is that bootdev and the
user vectors were carried over from a run of an OS image that is no
longer the one executing.

Clear the magic before the test. Every boot is a first boot, because
every boot is.

Splash and desktop unchanged in the emulator, which was always taking
the cold path: cart splash 8d837bd972e1f693, desktop 856ffb907a9819f6.

---
 bios/memory.S | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/memory.S b/bios/memory.S
index 19f930e..6896aae 100644
--- a/bios/memory.S
+++ b/bios/memory.S
@@ -172,6 +172,20 @@ memchk:
 
 memory_reused:
 #if CONF_DETECT_FIRST_BOOT_WITHOUT_MEMCONF
+#ifdef MACHINE_SEGACD
+        // There is no warm boot on this machine.
+        //
+        // Every start reads the whole OS image off the disc or out of
+        // the cartridge, so the code that is running has never run
+        // before. What does survive a reset is sub PRG-RAM -- the
+        // console does not clear it -- and the magic sitting in it
+        // belongs to a previous run of a program that is no longer the
+        // one here. Believing it cost the welcome screen on every reset
+        // (power-cycle and it came back, which is what made it look
+        // intermittent) and, less visibly, carried a stale bootdev and
+        // a stale set of user vectors into freshly loaded code.
+        clr.l   _warm_magic.w
+#endif
         // If _warm_magic == WARM_MAGIC, this is explicitly not a first boot
         lea     _warm_magic.w, a0
         move.l  #0x5741524D, d1         // WARM_MAGIC
